{
  "description": "Realtime wire frames the backend, web and mobile codecs must reproduce byte for byte, plus ordered frame sequences for the client coverage state machine.",
  "frame": "Bytes after the multiplex document name: a varuint message type, then the fields in the order listed below. A string is a varuint byte length and UTF-8 of at most 128 bytes. An integer is a varuint from 0 through 9007199254740991. A frame is malformed when its type differs, a field is truncated, a string exceeds 128 bytes or is not UTF-8, an integer exceeds the maximum, bytes trail the last field, accepted_sequence is 0 or checkpoint_sequence is above head_sequence.",
